COMPILATION OF: E49J1

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49J1

   1 a 0000 E49J1:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P4] NEGATED equality `^(rec.na = rec.nb)' -- FIRST
   4 a 0006      acceptance probe for `^ ( )' on a FIXED CHARACTER string head
   5 a 0006      (the numeric/fixed-bin NegL bank [C143] never touches
   6 a 0006      strings).  If accepted: H-D-inv predicts the un-negated
   7 a 0006      stacked head with skip C2 INVERTED to CA -- byte-identical to
   8 a 0006      the E49B5 golden (`rec.na ^= rec.nb') but names; H-D-simpl
   9 a 0006      (rewrite to ^=) gives the SAME bytes -- non-separable on this
  10 a 0006      shape, stated.  H-D-extra shows extra branch/helper bytes;
  11 a 0006      H-D-refuse is a DR boundary and then MY refusal stays.  NO De
  12 a 0006      Morgan assumption. */
  13 c 0006   dcl
  14 c 0006     1 rec,
  15 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  16 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  17 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  18 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  19 c 0006   if ^(rec.na = rec.nb) then k = 1;
  20 c 001D   put list('K=', k);
  21 c 003F   stop;
  22 a 0042 end E49J1;

CODE SIZE = 0042
DATA AREA = 000C
FREE SYMS = 3888
END  COMPILATION
